<article class="env-proposition" id="03ES">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03ES">Proposition <span data-tag="03ES">7.6.1.23</span> <span class="named">(Rewriting Limits as Products)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category, and let $\{  f_ i: K_ i \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\} _{i \in I}$ be a collection of diagrams, each of which admits a limit $X_ i = \varprojlim (f_ i)$. Set $K = {\coprod }_{i \in I} K_ i$, so that the collection $\{  f_ i \} _{i \in I}$ determines a diagram $f: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then an object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a limit of the diagram $f$ if it is a product of the collection of objects $\{  X_ i \} _{i \in I}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of (the dual of) Proposition <a data-tag="03DB" href="/tag/03DB">7.5.8.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
